comment 1587 "{\n  \"body\": \"PR stuck: no automation in this repository can move this pull request (`aaaaaaaa`).\\n\\nGitHub reports this PR `dirty` with **zero check runs**. That pair is the deadlock T-1368 names:\\n\\nA `dirty` PR has no merge ref; the gate runs on `pull_request`, which needs one,\\nso no gate ever starts; `gate` is a required check, so GitHub never calls the PR\\n`clean`; and `merge-ready.sh` merges only on `clean`. The lap is the one thing that\\ncan break the cycle, and it has not — either it refused a conflict it does not own,\\nor it has not run since this head was pushed.\\n\\nThe branch may well merge `dev` with no conflict at all. **GitHub never runs this\\nrepo's merge drivers** (T-0857), so a branch that merges cleanly in a clone is still\\nreported conflicting by the platform.\\n\\nWhat clears it, in the order to try:\\n\\n1. Dispatch **Chicago 4D — PR lap** with `only: 1587`. If it pushes, the gate runs\\n   on the merge and `merge-ready` takes it from there.\\n2. If the lap prints `REAL CONFLICT — left alone`, the conflict is in content no\\n   tool owns and it wants hands:\\n\\n```\\ngit fetch origin dev steward/t-1400-whatever\\ngit checkout -B steward/t-1400-whatever origin/steward/t-1400-whatever\\nchicago/4d/tools/setup-merge-drivers.sh   # or the merge will not resolve\\ngit merge origin/dev\\n# resolve the content conflicts by hand and git add them; derived files clear themselves:\\n( cd chicago/4d && node tools/rederive.mjs --resolve )\\n( cd chicago/4d && node tools/rederive.mjs --run && node tools/ticket.mjs reconcile --base origin/dev && ./tools/publish.sh )\\ngit add -A && git commit && git push origin HEAD:steward/t-1400-whatever\\n```\\n\\n3. Or close it and re-cut the work on a current `dev`.\\n\\nIf it is waiting on the OWNER on purpose, park it with `hold` — this reporter\\nreads labels first and leaves a held PR alone. If it is merely UNFINISHED, hand\\nit to the next run instead:\\n\\n    .github/steward/pr-rest.sh resume 1587 --why \\\"...\\\" --waits-on nothing\\n\\nwhich writes the reason where a machine and a person can both read it.\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\\n\"\n}\n"
